      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under N2, pieces of Eu metal (typically 5–10 mm diameter; 644 mg, 4.24 mmol) were reacted with excess dried 2-methoxyethanol at room temperature for 4 h to give an orange solution with no remaining metal. Excess HOCH2CH2OMe was removed under vacuum. The orange paste was taken into a nitrogen glovebox, dissolved in toluene, and centrifuged to remove a small amount of insoluble material (<10 mg). Toluene was removed in vacuo to an orange oil. Repeated dissolution in hexanes and drying by rotary evaporation gave orange powder 1. Isopiestic molecular-weight measurements in toluene indicate n > 10.",
