      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "From 2: a toluene solution of 2 (103 mg, 0.06 mmol in 5 mL) was added dropwise to Al2Me6 (34 mg, 0.27 mmol) in 2 mL of toluene at room temperature; the mixture lightened and bubbles formed. Concentration to ~2 mL gave a small amount of diffraction-quality crystals overnight (<20 mg). Alternative higher-yield route from 1: Al2Me6 (72 mg, 0.48 mmol) in 2 mL toluene in a Schlenk flask was cooled to −78 °C; HOCH2CH2OMe (75 mg, 0.989 mmol) in 2 mL toluene was added over 2 min. After 20 min the mixture was warmed to 0 °C and 1 (299 mg, 0.99 mmol) in 4 mL toluene was added. After 20 min the ice bath was removed and the mixture warmed to room temperature, then transferred to the glovebox. Additional Al2Me6 (72 mg, 0.50 mmol) in 2 mL toluene was added, giving insoluble material and an orange-to-yellow color change. Insoluble solids were removed by centrifugation; the supernatant was dried, washed twice with hexanes, and dried to microcrystalline 4, which was recrystallized from saturated hot toluene overnight (same unit cell as the first preparation).",
